  "title": "Antidirected trees in digraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "An antidirected tree is an orientation of a tree in which every vertex has either indegree 0 or outdergree 0.\n\nConjecture Let $D$ be a digraph. If $|A(D)| > (k-2) |V(D)|$, then $D$ contains every antidirected tree of order $k$.",
